            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0149" n="84" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/5090: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-23T15:00:00+03:00">October 23, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>608. I hear from an excellent first-hand source that Dejazmatch Wanda Wassan,
                    eldest son of Ras Kassa, and brother of Aberra mentioned in paragraph 4 of my
                    479, July 18<anchor n="53" xml:id="d90-f1"/> and later in telegrams rose against
                    the Italians in August in the province of Lasta northwest of Magdala. He had
                    simulated submission to the Italian authorities and had been given a command in
                    Lasta with headquarters at Lalibella where he gave effective protection to our
                    missionaries Mr. and Mrs. Oglesby. But since the end of August he and a
                    considerable body [of] followers have been in open rebellion and fighting
                    occurred near <pb facs="0150" n="85" xml:id="pg85"/> Lalibella as recently as
                    October 1. The Italians have confiscated or destroyed all his properties and are
                    rushing reinforcements into the region between Sokota and Lalibella where the
                    bulk of his forces are in hiding.</p>
                <p>Oglesbys apparently well and remaining at their station.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
